-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Protection): Improved Bloodrage, redesigned
-- ============================================================
-- TODO.md: "Improved Bloodrage (3, 2): Redesigned. Each time you take damage
--           while Bloodrage is active, the damage of your Shield Slam is
--           increased by 10%. Stacks 5 times. (2 ranks)"
--
-- Rank scaling: 5% and 10% per stack, five stacks at both ranks.  10% is the
-- rank 2 figure, as elsewhere in the Protection list.  At 2/2 with a full stack
-- that is +50% Shield Slam damage inside a 10 second window -- large, but it
-- costs the Bloodrage global, it costs health, and it only builds while you are
-- actually being hit.
--
-- Improved Bloodrage also MOVES to Tier 2 Col 3 in this batch (it was Tier 0
-- Col 0) -- see woa_2026_08_09_07.sql.  A talent that needs a rotation to spend
-- its ramp on does not belong in the first tier.
--
-- What it was: +25/50% to the rage Bloodrage generates.  Normalised rage
-- (Rage.Normalized = 1, Rage.FromDamageTaken = 0) already reshaped where a
-- tank's rage comes from, and buying a bigger one-off lump on a 60 second
-- cooldown was the least interesting answer available.  Bloodrage stays a rage
-- button; the talent now makes the window it opens matter.
--
-- "while Bloodrage is active" means aura 29131, not 2687.  2687 is instant --
-- SPELL_EFFECT_ENERGIZE plus SPELL_EFFECT_TRIGGER_SPELL -- and 29131 is the 10
-- second periodic-energize aura it triggers.  That distinction is the entire
-- reason this talent needs a script (spell_warr_imp_bloodrage,
-- modules/world_of_alonecraft/src/WarriorProtGates.cpp); its header explains
-- why neither spell_proc nor the DBC's CasterAuraSpell can express "while".
--
-- Stack scaling is automatic and needs no help: AuraEffect::CalculateAmount
-- ends with amount *= GetBase()->GetStackAmount() (SpellAuraEffects.cpp:580)
-- for every aura type.  So the base points hold the PER-STACK value and the
-- buff-bar tooltip uses $s1, which the client multiplies by the current stack
-- count on its own.  Writing "10% per stack" into SpellToolTip0 would be a bug,
-- not a safe fallback -- it would defeat scaling the client does for free.  The
-- spellbook description is the opposite case: it is read with no stack count to
-- scale against, so it says "per stack" explicitly.
--
-- The modifier is masked to SpellFamilyFlags1 = 512, which is Shield Slam and
-- only Shield Slam across all eight ranks
-- (gen_sql.py classmask --family 4 --spells 23922,...,47488).  That is the same
-- bit SpellEffects.cpp:350 uses to find Shield Slam.
--
-- spell_proc: ProcFlags 40 = 0x8 PROC_FLAG_TAKEN_MELEE_AUTO_ATTACK
-- | 0x20 PROC_FLAG_TAKEN_SPELL_MELEE_DMG_CLASS -- "each time you take damage".
-- SpellPhaseMask 2 is mandatory for the 0x20 half.  Chance 0 = always; the
-- script supplies the only condition.
--
-- Spells:
--   12301 / 12818    = Improved Bloodrage ranks 1-2
--   200647 / 200648  = Bloodrage (the stacking Shield Slam buff), new
--   29131            = Bloodrage aura (the gate, untouched)
-- ============================================================

